// RoPE parity smoke test.
//
// Golden values below are produced by the *real* HF `transformers`
// rotate_half/apply_rotary_pos_emb implementation (torch 2.9.0,
// transformers 5.5.0, both installed in this environment - see
// docs/repro notes for the exact generation script), evaluated in
// float64, on a fixed 64-dim vector at head_dim=64/rope_theta=1e6 (the
// real Qwen2.5 dense-transformer shape), for position in {0, 1, 100,
// 8192}: identity at position 0, a small position, a mid-range position,
// and a large position exercising the wide-angle branch of the range
// reduction. The int32 quantized input vector (scale=1000) is fixed and
// untouched between the Python reference run and this Cheng harness.

